{"data": [{"author_id": "2465283662", "created_at": "2026-10-28T15:21:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115463926184116648"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Join the discussion on this paper page", "display_url": "huggingface.co/papers/2610.37…", "end": 100, "expanded_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.37666", "images": [{"height": 648, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115287651104464896/73hkSRSB?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115287651104464896/73hkSRSB?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 77, "status": 200, "title": "Paper page - ThinkWorld: World Imagination Reinforces Chain-of-Dynamics Reasoning", "unwound_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.37666", "url": "https://t.co/DCyVCUs3wa"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/vb94kpw6Bc", "end": 124, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2115463926184116648/video/1", "media_key": "13_2115463824480288768", "start": 101, "url": "https://t.co/vb94kpw6Bc"}]}, "id": "2115463926184116648", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 55, "impression_count": 16860, "like_count": 115, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 17}, "text": "ThinkWorld\n\nWorld Imagination Reinforces Chain-of-Dynamics Reasoning\n\npaper: https://t.co/DCyVCUs3wa https://t.co/vb94kpw6Bc", "url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2115463926184116648"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-28T15:03:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115459422696636806"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/XMpoXbTDCG", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2115459422696636806/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115459420263940097", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/XMpoXbTDCG"}]}, "id": "2115459422696636806", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 89, "impression_count": 31227, "like_count": 191, "quote_count": 6, "reply_count": 43, "retweet_count": 15}, "text": "ALERT🚨: The number of tokens that can be cached can increase by 20-40%🚀 by enabling DRAM KVCache offloading optimization at 12-16 concurrent agentic sessions. A B200 only has 180 GB of HBM, and after weight storage, only 100 GB of HBM per chip remains for KVCache.\n\nTHIS IS NOT https://t.co/XMpoXbTDCG", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2115459422696636806"}, {"author_id": "12497", "created_at": "2026-10-28T14:05:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115444742595260551"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "I’ve written before about how November 2025 was an inflection point for coding agents—the point where Opus 4.5 and GPT-5.1 crossed a tipping point that meant their respective coding agents …", "display_url": "simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/28/vi…", "end": 205, "expanded_url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/28/vibe-game-development/", "images": [{"height": 1000, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115443204439105537/ljiAX8MN?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1728}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115443204439105537/ljiAX8MN?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 182, "status": 200, "title": "The October inflection point for vibe game development", "unwound_url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/28/vibe-game-development/", "url": "https://t.co/aPsJ14RHR0"}]}, "id": "2115444742595260551", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 762, "impression_count": 105853, "like_count": 1314, "quote_count": 70, "reply_count": 371, "retweet_count": 74}, "text": "I think October represents another inflection point in capabilities for coding agents and the models that drive them: Claude Opus 5.5 can now build video games that are actually fun https://t.co/aPsJ14RHR0", "url": "https://x.com/simonw/status/2115444742595260551"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-28T13:35:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115437422146130032"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/DbvE6Tk5qL", "end": 265, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2115437422146130032/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115437419956670464", "start": 242, "url": "https://t.co/DbvE6Tk5qL"}]}, "id": "2115437422146130032", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 20, "impression_count": 9713, "like_count": 119, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 40, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Private benchmarks often show open models are further behind, but the problem with private benchmarks is you don’t have the community to squash the inevitable bugs for you. I'm 50/50 on if I think private or open-source is the best approach. https://t.co/DbvE6Tk5qL", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2115437422146130032"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-28T13:00:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115428494515777629"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A sort of review of the benchmarking industry and what's missing.", "display_url": "interconnects.ai/p/artificial-a…", "end": 266, "expanded_url": "https://www.interconnects.ai/p/artificial-analysis-v5-and-the-benchmarkers", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115428497808326656/3Tlfg566?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115428497808326656/3Tlfg566?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 243, "status": 200, "title": "Artificial Analysis v5 and the benchmarker's dilemma", "unwound_url": "https://www.interconnects.ai/p/artificial-analysis-v5-and-the-benchmarkers", "url": "https://t.co/7lT09ijAqj"}]}, "id": "2115428494515777629", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 69, "impression_count": 10882, "like_count": 199, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 22, "retweet_count": 23}, "text": "Open models' demise has been greatly exaggerated, but the previous AA index did flatter them. As an industry we need more specific intelligence indices, as LLMs are used in vastly different tasks.\n\nMy meta-review on the benchmarking industry.\nhttps://t.co/7lT09ijAqj", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2115428494515777629"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-28T10:21:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115388473507184867"], "id": "2115388473507184867", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 21, "impression_count": 14396, "like_count": 164, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 33, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "I feel a need to defend the AAv5 index and open models at the same time. Benchmarking is messier, more opinionated, and trickier than most people give credit to.", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2115388473507184867"}, {"author_id": "985281530070265862", "created_at": "2026-10-28T00:57:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115246475391471817"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "The SemiAnalysis Datacenter Industry Model: site-level forecasts of AI datacenter capacity and power for more than 6,000 colocation and hyperscale facilities and 200+ companies, 2017 to 2032, with capacity and capex by hyperscaler and power supply-demand by region, built from permits, property records, and satellite imagery and updated quarterly.", "display_url": "semianalysis.com/datacenter-ind…", "end": 91, "expanded_url": "https://semianalysis.com/datacenter-industry-model/", "images": [{"height": 1927, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115246523634311168/bwKXa6wV?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1240}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115246523634311168/bwKXa6wV?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 68, "status": 200, "title": "Datacenter Industry Model", "unwound_url": "https://semianalysis.com/datacenter-industry-model/", "url": "https://t.co/BwJmRQVd0E"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/sxyMWuNAl3", "end": 115, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/dylan522p/status/2115246475391471817/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115246234990686208", "start": 92, "url": "https://t.co/sxyMWuNAl3"}]}, "id": "2115246475391471817", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 56, "impression_count": 32562, "like_count": 147, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 21, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "Re OpenAI TPU announcements, SemiAnalysis clients had this already.\nhttps://t.co/BwJmRQVd0E https://t.co/sxyMWuNAl3", "url": "https://x.com/dylan522p/status/2115246475391471817"}, {"author_id": "1482581556", "created_at": "2026-10-27T23:59:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115232001275924722"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/GoogleDeepMind…", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/2115114028338962672", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/NAAo2aTCey"}]}, "id": "2115232001275924722", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 660, "impression_count": 230505, "like_count": 4716, "quote_count": 72, "reply_count": 245, "retweet_count": 387}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115114028338962672", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Very excited to share Genie 4, our incredible interactive world model, bringing together real-time physics, reasoning, and audio! Simulations within simulations, makes you wonder just how deep the rabbit hole goes... I have a feeling we will be finding out soon enough... https://t.co/NAAo2aTCey", "url": "https://x.com/demishassabis/status/2115232001275924722"}, {"author_id": "1353836358901501952", "created_at": "2026-10-27T22:20:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115207004293853358"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 43, "id": "61583656", "start": 37, "username": "USGSA"}], "urls": [{"description": "Anthropic is an AI safety and research company that's working to build reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems.", "display_url": "anthropic.com/news/expanding…", "end": 195, "expanded_url": "https://www.anthropic.com/news/expanding-partnership-gsa", "images": [{"height": 1080, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115207005828972544/NnQuK9VS?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115207005828972544/NnQuK9VS?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 172, "status": 200, "title": "Expanding our partnership with GSA to bring Claude to all levels of government", "unwound_url": "https://www.anthropic.com/news/expanding-partnership-gsa", "url": "https://t.co/p0lA6cP2y1"}]}, "id": "2115207004293853358", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 326, "impression_count": 468385, "like_count": 2230, "quote_count": 130, "reply_count": 342, "retweet_count": 135}, "text": "We're expanding our partnership with @USGSA. Under a new OneGov agreement, we are bringing Claude to federal, state, local, tribal, and territorial governments at 40% off.\nhttps://t.co/p0lA6cP2y1", "url": "https://x.com/AnthropicAI/status/2115207004293853358"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:35:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115195793648812162"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/OracleCloud/st…", "end": 83, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/OracleCloud/status/2115121377187344641", "start": 60, "url": "https://t.co/7vFiRSX7dd"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/rHlGZ5LQG4", "end": 107, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2115195793648812162/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115195790612201472", "start": 84, "url": "https://t.co/rHlGZ5LQG4"}]}, "id": "2115195793648812162", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 114, "impression_count": 90616, "like_count": 1271, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 25, "retweet_count": 49}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115121377187344641", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "PoV of Jensen after reading TPUs are coming to Oracle Cloud\nhttps://t.co/7vFiRSX7dd https://t.co/rHlGZ5LQG4", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2115195793648812162"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-27T21:25:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115193271085637739"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/giotto_ai/stat…", "end": 97, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/giotto_ai/status/2115100162204856795", "start": 74, "url": "https://t.co/pNNw5N6iqK"}]}, "id": "2115193271085637739", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 20, "impression_count": 23790, "like_count": 104, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 22, "retweet_count": 10}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115100162204856795", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "People underestimate how much money is left to get thrown at sovereign ai https://t.co/pNNw5N6iqK", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2115193271085637739"}, {"author_id": "1529761561170124800", "created_at": "2026-10-27T20:57:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115186242459767006"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/zRfXsCm6yK", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EpochAIResearch/status/2115186242459767006/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115186239494320128", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/zRfXsCm6yK"}]}, "id": "2115186242459767006", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 201, "impression_count": 87020, "like_count": 570, "quote_count": 31, "reply_count": 24, "retweet_count": 107}, "text": "Since 2022, 72% of the world’s AI compute has ended up in the US and about 10% in China.\n\nAnd the US share keeps growing. It acquired around 60% of new compute each year from 2022 to 2024, then 72% in 2025, and 78% in the first half of 2026.\n\nThis data comes from our interactive https://t.co/zRfXsCm6yK", "url": "https://x.com/EpochAIResearch/status/2115186242459767006"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "2465283662", "name": "AK", "username": "_akhaliq"}, {"id": "1745106082790318080", "name": "SemiAnalysis", "username": "SemiAnalysis_"}, {"id": "12497", "name": "Simon Willison", "username": "simonw"}, {"id": "2939913921", "name": "Nathan Lambert", "username": "natolambert"}, {"id": "985281530070265862", "name": "Dylan Patel", "username": "dylan522p"}, {"id": "1482581556", "name": "Demis Hassabis", "username": "demishassabis"}, {"id": "1353836358901501952", "name": "Anthropic", "username": "AnthropicAI"}, {"id": "1529761561170124800", "name": "Epoch AI", "username": "EpochAIResearch"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2115463926184116648", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlxnw